# WHYspace Agent Communication Model

## Overview

Programs in WHYspace are not isolated — they communicate through an **internal message bus**. This enables complex multi-agent workflows where programs collaborate, share data, and trigger actions in response to events.

---

## Message Bus Architecture

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                  MESSAGE BUS                        │
│                                                     │
│  publish(message) → [Topic] → subscribers receive  │
│                                                     │
│  request(from, to, payload) → response promise     │
│                                                     │
│  pipe(from, to, transform) → continuous stream     │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## Message Format

```typescript
interface AgentMessage {
  id: string;                    // unique message ID
  type: MessageType;
  from: string;                  // source program ID
  to: string | '*';             // target or broadcast
  topic?: string;               // for pub/sub routing
  payload: unknown;
  timestamp: number;
  correlationId?: string;       // pairs request/response
  ttl?: number;                 // time-to-live in ms
  priority?: 'low' | 'normal' | 'high';
}

type MessageType =
  | 'request'       // Expect a response
  | 'response'      // Reply to a request
  | 'event'         // Fire-and-forget notification
  | 'broadcast'     // To all subscribers
  | 'pipe_chunk'    // Streaming data segment
  | 'pipe_end'      // Stream terminated
  | 'error';        // Error response
```

---

## Communication Patterns

### 1. Request/Response

Synchronous-style communication between programs:

```typescript
// Program A: Memory Vault
const { results } = await kernel.request({
  to: 'research-agent',
  type: 'request',
  payload: {
    action: 'summarize',
    text: selectedText
  }
});

// Program B: Research Agent handles it
kernel.onRequest('research-agent', async (msg) => {
  if (msg.payload.action === 'summarize') {
    const summary = await summarize(msg.payload.text);
    return { type: 'response', payload: { summary } };
  }
});
```

### 2. Event Pub/Sub

Fire-and-forget notifications:

```typescript
// Code Studio emits an event on file save
kernel.emit('file:saved', {
  path: '/src/components/App.tsx',
  size: 1243
});

// Workflow Automator listens
kernel.on('file:saved', (event) => {
  if (event.payload.path.endsWith('.tsx')) {
    kernel.launch('code-studio', { action: 'lint', file: event.payload.path });
  }
});
```

### 3. Program Piping

Stream data directly between programs:

```typescript
// Pipe Research Agent output into Core Chat
kernel.pipe({
  from: 'research-agent',
  to: 'core-chat',
  transform: (data) => ({
    role: 'assistant',
    content: `**Research Findings:**\n\n${data.content}`
  })
});

// Cancel the pipe
kernel.unpipe(pipeId);
```

### 4. Workflow Orchestration

The Workflow Automator coordinates multi-step pipelines:

```typescript
const workflow = await kernel.createWorkflow({
  name: 'Daily Research Brief',
  steps: [
    { program: 'research-agent', action: 'gather', params: { topics: ['AI', 'quantum'] } },
    { program: 'research-agent', action: 'summarize' },
    { program: 'core-chat', action: 'format', params: { style: 'brief' } },
    { program: 'voice-nexus', action: 'tts', params: { voice: 'en-US-Neural2-F' } }
  ],
  trigger: { type: 'schedule', cron: '0 8 * * 1-5' }
});
```

---

## Event Reference

### System Events

| Event | Payload | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `system:boot` | `{ version }` | OS started |
| `system:shutdown` | `{}` | OS shutting down |
| `system:provider:changed` | `{ from, to }` | AI provider switched |
| `system:memory:warning` | `{ usage, limit }` | Memory threshold crossed |
| `system:error` | `{ code, message }` | Unhandled system error |

### Program Events

| Event | Payload | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `program:launched` | `{ id, pid }` | Program started |
| `program:terminated` | `{ id, pid, reason }` | Program stopped |
| `program:error` | `{ id, pid, error }` | Program encountered error |
| `program:state:changed` | `{ id, from, to }` | Program state transition |

### AI Events

| Event | Payload | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `ai:stream:start` | `{ id, provider, model }` | AI stream started |
| `ai:stream:chunk` | `{ id, delta }` | Token received |
| `ai:stream:done` | `{ id, usage }` | Stream completed |
| `ai:stream:error` | `{ id, error }` | Stream error |
| `ai:tool:called` | `{ tool, args, result }` | AI used a tool |

### Memory Events

| Event | Payload | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `memory:stored` | `{ key, program }` | New memory entry |
| `memory:deleted` | `{ key }` | Memory deleted |
| `memory:search:done` | `{ query, count }` | Search completed |

---

## Bus Implementation

```typescript
class MessageBus {
  private handlers: Map<string, Set<Handler>>;
  private pending: Map<string, PromiseWithResolvers>;

  publish(msg: AgentMessage): void {
    const handlers = this.handlers.get(msg.to) ?? new Set();
    const wildcard = this.handlers.get('*') ?? new Set();
    
    for (const handler of [...handlers, ...wildcard]) {
      handler(msg);
    }
  }

  async request(to: string, payload: unknown, timeout = 30000): Promise<unknown> {
    const correlationId = crypto.randomUUID();
    const { promise, resolve, reject } = Promise.withResolvers();
    
    this.pending.set(correlationId, { resolve, reject });
    
    this.publish({
      id: crypto.randomUUID(),
      type: 'request',
      from: 'current-program',
      to,
      payload,
      correlationId,
      timestamp: Date.now()
    });

    // Timeout
    setTimeout(() => {
      if (this.pending.has(correlationId)) {
        this.pending.delete(correlationId);
        reject(new Error('Request timed out'));
      }
    }, timeout);

    return promise;
  }

  respond(correlationId: string, payload: unknown): void {
    const pending = this.pending.get(correlationId);
    if (pending) {
      pending.resolve(payload);
      this.pending.delete(correlationId);
    }
  }
}
```
